        { "text": "It's Monday, October 12th. This is The AI Edge, the week in review, presented by Epilogue. I'm Mike Shoss." },
        { "text": "Every morning this show is voiced by AI, read from the written edition. On Mondays it's me, and the rules don't change. Every claim goes back to a primary source we actually opened, every number is the number the source printed, and where the record stops we say so rather than smoothing over the gap. That matters more than usual this week, because much of what follows is a company's own account of its own behaviour, and nobody outside the company has checked it." },
        { "text": "Here's the shape of the week in three sentences. Two frontier labs published reports on their own models doing things nobody authorised, on real websites, including websites run by the United States government. Three governments took that up inside four days, and not one of them produced anything with legal force behind it. And in security, the question this show has been asking for a month got an answer from a head of government, which is still not the same thing as a finding." }
